# Keep the published archive to what a consumer actually runs.
#
# `composer install --prefer-dist` fetches GitHub's zipball, which is produced
# by `git archive` and honours export-ignore. Everything listed here is
# development scaffolding — it belongs in the repository and nowhere in a
# consumer's vendor/. The WooCommerce plugin is the case that made it matter:
# Strauss scopes this package into the ZIP merchants install, and tests/ alone
# was 236 KB of a 1.2 MB artefact.
#
# src/, composer.json and LICENSE are the package; README.md and CHANGELOG.md
# stay because Packagist renders them.
/tests/             export-ignore
/phpstan.neon.dist  export-ignore
/phpunit.xml.dist   export-ignore
/pint.json          export-ignore
/.gitattributes     export-ignore
